on {:value "1937"} "30 kilometres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "1938"} "50 kilometres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "1939"} "4 × 10 kilometres Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "1943"} "5 kilometres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "1944"} "10 kilometres, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "1922"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "1933"} "1960"] "\n" [:option {:value "1957"} "1968"] "\n" [:option {:value "1969"} "1972"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/202"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "3 × 5 kilometres Relay, Women" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} " 7 February 1964 — 9:30"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/59"} "Langlaufstadion, Seefeld"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/1945"} "24 from 8 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: ?" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 64 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 39 m" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 150 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "In the two earlier games with the cross country relay for women on the program, the highly favored Soviet women had surprisingly not been able to win a gold medal. In 1956 they lost to Finland, and in 1960 Sweden took a most unexpected gold medal. The Soviets had won three World Championships in a row, in 1954, 1958 and 1962, and were also the big favorite for the gold medal this time."] "\n\n" [:p {} "And this time the relay went on as expected. The experienced " [:a {:href "/athletes/81534"} "Alevtina Kolchina"] " made no mistakes on the first leg and had a 36 seconds lead over Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/81770"} "Barbro Martinsson."] " at the first exchange. But Finland’s young " [:a {:href "/athletes/82139"} "Senja Pusula"] " ran into trouble on her first leg and reached the exchange in fourth place, almost two and a half minutes behind the leader and 1:11 behind Germany in third place. " [:a {:href "/athletes/81807"} "Yevdokiya Mekshilo"] " and double Olympic Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/80720"} "Klavdiya Boyarskikh"] " increased the Soviet lead on the last two legs, and the Soviet Union won the gold with a comfortable margin, over two minutes ahead of Sweden. On the second leg, Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/81831"} "Toini Pöysti"] " was able to overtake Germany, and Finland secured the bronze medal almost two minutes ahead of Germany, but 1:18 behind Sweden."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Exchange"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5"] [:td {} "Soviet Union"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "59:20.2"] [:td {} "– (–)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Lead-Off"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5-1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/81534"} "Alevtina Kolchina"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "21:17.9"] [:td {} "21:17.9 (1)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2nd Leg"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5-2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/81807"} "Yevdokiya Mekshilo"] " "] [:td {}] [:td {} "19:08.5"] [:td {} "40:26.4 (1)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "Anchor"] [:td {:class "bib"} "5-3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/80720